From: Adam Hillson <598804+BadAd84@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] glm lanes: correct 0026's SHARED_DRAFTS gating and drop the unported-lever test

0026 gated `allocate_shared_drafts` on `block and cuda.ovn.on("SHARED_DRAFTS")`. The
source commit's line is `drafting and cuda.ovn.on("SHARED_DRAFTS")`, and the difference
matters: `drafting` is the MTP head, which is true with no drafter loaded, so 0026's
gating turned shared draft allocation off in that case. Corrected to the source line.

The pin's own `copy_drafts_cuda_test` asserts the opposite default for GLM
(`allocate_shared_drafts = true`), which is the behaviour TF_GLM_OVN_SHARED_DRAFTS
deliberately replaces: docs/PARITY.md records the flip (7b41f0d26) - the depth rule is
the default again and the core allocator sits behind the knob, measured at P4 with equal
tokens. That literal is therefore updated for glm_mtp/glm_block to false, the way 0024
updated the other adapters, rather than reverting the knob.

`TF_GLM_OVN_DEPTH_FULL and SHARED_COPY: each knob reaches the round loop's config` is
deleted: both levers live in `config.Config` fields the port does not carry, so after
0024's repair the test asserted the wrong lever and a tautology. Its sibling
`TF_GLM_OVN_SHARED_ROWS` assertion was already folded to the comptime bound for the
same reason.

Gates on pin+0001..0027: check-native-cuda-host green, whole-tree fmt green, lean
base-vs-head 0 new, test-cuda-host 8 to 6 named failures with no new ones.
diff --git a/zig/src/families/glm/cuda_lanes.zig b/zig/src/families/glm/cuda_lanes.zig
index 3b5dc5e7a..11ac31746 100644
--- a/zig/src/families/glm/cuda_lanes.zig
+++ b/zig/src/families/glm/cuda_lanes.zig
@@ -136,7 +136,7 @@ pub const Lanes = struct {
             // TF_GLM_OVN_WIN_FREE: a shared round's windows take no cost model, so they fill likeliest-first
             .free_shared = block and cuda.ovn.on("WIN_FREE"),
             // TF_GLM_OVN_SHARED_DRAFTS: shared rounds draft from the core allocator instead of the depth rule
-            .allocate_shared_drafts = block and cuda.ovn.on("SHARED_DRAFTS"),
+            .allocate_shared_drafts = drafting and cuda.ovn.on("SHARED_DRAFTS"), // the depth rule is the default
             // TF_GLM_OVN_PLAIN_MARGIN: hundredths; a draft must beat plain rounds by this (0: the core's 105)
             .plain_margin = @as(f64, @floatFromInt(cuda.ovn.int("PLAIN_MARGIN", 0) catch 0)) / 100.0,
             .hidden_rows = sharing,
